# Vantage Movers Server Organization

- `vantage-main-server` is the Vercel-hosted Express REST API for Vantage Movers. Production URL: `https://vantage-movers-main-server.vercel.app`.
- Runtime API code belongs under `src/`. Operational/personal tooling belongs under `scripts/`. Architecture, schema, workflow, and migration notes belong under `docs/`.
- Before changing write paths, identify `TEST_MODE`, selected Mongo DB, target Google Sheet env vars, and whether the code can touch CRM, Postman, or production customer data.

## API Launch Map

- Start request tracing at `api/index.ts`: Express app setup, health/db probes, logging, CORS/body parsing, and route mounting.
- `src/routes/` owns HTTP boundaries. Keep routes thin: authenticate, parse with Zod, call services, format responses, and avoid business logic.
- `src/routes/v1.routes.ts` is the main surface: public `/api/v1/*` writes/reads, extension-facing browse/enrichment/reconciliation, Granot CSV uploads, admin browse/search/export/analytics, catalog/CPL admin, sheet-sync ops, and observability admin. Mounted last so cron/webhook routes stay separate.
- `src/routes/extension-auth.routes.ts` serves `/api/v1/extension/auth/*` (login, refresh, me, logout) without `x-api-secret`; mounted inside `v1.routes.ts` before the auth guard.
- Cron/webhook routes mount directly from `api/index.ts`: RingCentral webhooks + cron, Granot webhook capture, sheet-sync drain cron, notification digest cron.
- `src/validation/` owns request/operation schemas. `src/validation/v1.validation.ts` is the public v1 barrel; detailed schemas live in `src/validation/v1/`.
- `src/models/` owns runtime Mongoose schemas and shared schema helpers. Mongo/API fields stay `snake_case`; only Google Sheets projections produce owner-facing Title Case columns.
- `src/config/domain/` owns mode-aware domain configuration (`runtime`, `sources`, `sheets`, `cpl`, `sheetSync`, `granotCsv`, `observability`, `googleAuth`, `constants`). Re-exported by `src/config/domain.ts`. Add source companies, sheet tabs, headers, CPL rules, Mongo database names, and Google auth env selection here instead of scattering `process.env` reads.
- `src/middleware/` owns request guards and request-level behavior: `requireApiSecret` (`requireVantageAuth`), HTTP logging.
- `src/auth/extension/` owns Granot browser-extension login, JWT access/refresh tokens, password hashing, and `ExtensionUser` lookup.
- `src/utils/` owns small shared helpers under `logging/`, `googleSheets/`, `location/`, plus top-level helpers such as `easternTime.ts` and CSV serialization.
- `src/db.ts` is the shared Mongo connection helper. Runtime code should reuse it and preserve the `TEST_MODE` database boundary.
- `api/queues/sheet-sync-consumer.ts` is the queue consumer entry for sheet-sync wake-ups when `SHEET_SYNC_MODE=queued`.

## Auth Surface

- Protected `/api/v1/*` routes accept, in order: primary `x-api-secret`, extension Bearer token (owner role only for data routes; employees are rejected), or scoped API keys from `VANTAGE_SCOPED_API_KEYS` (route + source-company constrained).
- Extension auth is separate from admin secret auth. Granot Sync uses Bearer tokens; website forms and internal scripts typically use `x-api-secret` or scoped keys.
- Successful auth attaches `req.vantageAuth` (`secret`, `scoped_key`, or `user`). Do not bypass this guard for new v1 endpoints.

## Services — Core Domain

Mongo is the source of truth. Domain services own business behavior and side effects; prefer importing from the domain folder, not legacy barrels.

- `src/services/leads/` — Form/call lead CRUD, duplicate quarantine, phone/name/source-company helpers, location enrichment, source-lead lookup. Models: `FormLead`, `CallLead`.
- `src/services/agents/` — Receiver-agent attribution from Granot CRM usernames (`receiverAgentCrmUsername.ts`). Used by call-lead enrichment/reconciliation sync and supports extension form-lead PATCH provenance. Model: `Agent` (`granot_crm_username`, virtual `form_leads_received` / `call_leads_received`).
- `src/services/bookings/` — Booked-lead CRUD, booking-from-source, referral bookings, leadless bookings, booking mirror updates, source-company resolution for attached leads. Model: `BookedLead`.
- `src/services/cancellations/` — Cancelled-lead CRUD, cancellation resolver, sheet mirror helpers. Model: `CancelledLead`.
- `src/services/customers/` — Customer CRUD and customer upsert from lead/booking flows. Model: `Customer`.
- `src/services/catalog/` — Admin catalog CRUD for agents and merchants (`/api/v1/admin/catalog/*`, `/admin/agents`, `/admin/merchants`). Models: `Agent`, `Merchant`.
- `src/services/cpl/` — DB-backed CPL rate admin reads/updates. Model: `CplRate`. Resolution helpers also live in `src/config/domain/cpl.ts`.
- `src/services/testimonials/` — Public testimonial listing for marketing site. Model: `Testimonial`.

## Services — Extension & Granot Workflows

These integrate the Granot browser extension with production leads.

- `src/services/search/` — Paginated browse (`GET /form-leads`, `/call-leads`) and POST search used by the extension Search workspace. Populates receiver-agent snapshots.
- `src/services/enrichment/` — Call-lead enrichment preview/sync from Granot Follow Up Estimates rows (`/call-leads/enrichment/*`). Matches leads by phone/job metadata; can set `receiver_agent` from row `granot_crm_username` when unset.
- `src/services/reconciliation/` — Booked call-lead reconciliation preview/sync from Granot Booked Jobs rows (`/call-leads/booked-reconciliation/*`). Updates booking chain or call-lead-only paths; same receiver-agent matching rules as enrichment.
- `src/services/granotCrmCsv/` — Granot CRM CSV source registry, S3/storage ingest, and sync runs triggered by the extension CSV workspace (`/granot-crm/csv/*`). Models: `GranotCrmSource`, `GranotCrmCsvIngestion`, `GranotCrmSyncRun`. Config: `src/config/domain/granotCsv.ts`.

Form-lead sync from the extension uses public `PATCH /api/v1/form-leads/:id` (including optional `receiver_agent` provenance fields validated in `src/validation/v1/leads.validation.ts`).

## Services — External Integrations

- `src/services/crm/` — Granot CRM submission for inbound form leads (`crm.service.ts`, payload builders, `crmConfig.ts`). Invoked from form-lead create/update paths; not a route boundary.
- `src/services/granotWebhooks/` — Authenticated, schema-flexible capture of Granot lead-created, priority-updated, and booking-status webhook receipts. Initial capture is durable only and does not mutate lead or booking state.
- `src/services/googleSheets/` — Google Sheets API client, tab/target resolution, row lookup, batch sync/delete, diagnostics. `projections/` maps Mongo documents to owner-facing sheet rows (`formLeadRow`, `callLeadRow`, `bookedLeadRow`, shared `cells.ts`).
- `src/services/sheetSync/` — Write-behind outbox for Google Sheets. Domain writes enqueue jobs (`sheetSyncOutbox.service.ts`); coordinator runs transactional Mongo writes + intent persistence (`sheetSyncCoordinator.ts`); drainer batches jobs with leases/quota limits (`drainer/`); queue publish/wakeup (`sheetSyncQueue.service.ts`). Models: `SheetSyncJob`, `SheetSyncRun`, `SheetSyncAttempt`, `SheetSyncLease`, `SheetSyncQuotaBucket`. Config: `src/config/domain/sheetSync.ts`.
- `src/services/googleAuth/` — Service-account credential loading for Sheets (separate from `googleSheets/auth.ts` client wiring).
- `src/services/googleDriveOAuth/` — Owner-authorized Google Drive connection, encrypted refresh-token persistence, one-time OAuth state, and creation of owner-requested spreadsheets. HTTP endpoints live in `src/routes/google-drive-oauth.routes.ts`.
- `src/services/googleMaps/` — Geocoding health checks for admin (`/admin/google-maps/geocoding-health`).

## Services — RingCentral

- `src/routes/ringcentral-webhook.routes.ts`, `ringcentral-webhook-local.routes.ts`, and `ringcentral-cron.routes.ts` are HTTP/cron boundaries only; keep qualification, persistence, and lead-write behavior in services.
- `src/services/ringcentral/` owns RingCentral auth/client code, token stores, webhook capture/normalization, candidate/session aggregation, Call Log sync, Analytics reconciliation, idempotency, duplicate detection, and shadow/real call-lead ingest.
- `ringcentral-config.ts` is the single source for RingCentral env toggles, collection names, collection mode, duplicate window, cron lookback/overlap, and lead write posture.
- `call-lead-sources.ts` owns mapped inbound numbers and source-company attribution. Do not duplicate those mappings in routes, scripts, or tests.
- `ringcentral-call-lead-ingest.service.ts` is the shared promotion path for webhook and Call Log qualified calls. Do not create RingCentral `call_leads` directly from route, webhook, cron, or script code.

## Services — Admin, Analytics, Observability

- `src/services/admin/` — Production vs historical scope (`adminScope.service.ts`), paginated browse/detail/export (`adminBrowse.service.ts`, `adminExport.service.ts`), global search/facets (`adminSearch.service.ts`, `adminFacets.service.ts`), sheet-sync health/job/run admin (`adminSheetSync.service.ts`), agent browse metrics.
- `src/services/analytics/` — Admin analytics reports (summary, revenue, source/agent performance, funnel, cancellation, geographic, lead-cost) plus overview and agent-sales report/export helpers. Mounted under `/api/v1/admin/analytics/*` and `/admin/reports/agent-sales`.
- `src/services/observability/` — Operational events, incidents, notification policy, digest/retry behavior, admin overview reads, and operational report generation. Runtime schemas: `OperationalEvent`, `OperationalIncident`, `NotificationDelivery`, `OperationalReportRun` via `observabilityModelFactory.ts`. Config: `src/config/domain/observability.ts`.
- Notification digest cron mounts from `src/routes/notification-cron.routes.ts`; keep it a thin authenticated boundary around observability services.
- Admin browse resources: `form-leads`, `call-leads`, `booked-leads`, `cancelled-leads`, `customers`, `agents` — each with list, detail, and CSV export under `/api/v1/admin/...`. Also: global search, facets, catalog agents/merchants, CPL rates, sheet-sync ops, analytics reports, observability suite.
- `database_scope=production|historical|combined` is supported where appropriate. Detail endpoints reject `combined`; historical scope is read-only; combined is for search/export-style reads.
- Do not add `/api/v1/admin` delete routes for core leads/bookings/customers. Admin write workflows should continue to use existing public v1 write services so Google Sheet sync behavior is preserved. Observability collections are the exception and have explicit admin delete endpoints.

## Legacy Compatibility Barrels

Prefer direct domain imports in new code. These re-export moved implementations so routes and scripts keep compiling:

- `src/services/v1.service.ts` — leads, bookings, cancellations, customers, sheet-sync schedulers, `V1ServiceError`.
- `src/services/formLeadSearch.service.ts`, `callLeadSearch.service.ts` → `search/`.
- `src/services/callLeadEnrichment.service.ts` → `enrichment/`.
- `src/services/bookedCallLeadReconciliation.service.ts` → `reconciliation/`.
- `src/services/crm.service.ts` → `crm/` (if present as barrel).

## Cross-Cutting Write Flow

Most mutating domain services follow the same integration pattern:

1. Validate input (route Zod schema + service guards).
2. Persist Mongo change (often in a transaction when sheet sync is involved).
3. Enqueue or schedule Google Sheet sync (`schedule*SheetSync`, `runSheetSyncWrite`, `persistSheetSyncIntent`).
4. Optionally trigger CRM submit (form leads), customer upsert (bookings), CPL recompute, or observability events.

When touching a write path, trace which downstream targets it affects before editing.

## Script Launch Map

- Run scripts through `package.json` commands so `.env` loading and `tsx` invocation remain consistent.
- `scripts/dev_ops/` — Personal/admin DB operations, extension-user seeding, agent CRM username backfills, duplicate audits, production patches, webhook probes. Treat as potentially destructive even when names sound local.
- `scripts/historical/` — Historical backfill, reconciliation, diagnostics, analytics, and repairs. `scripts/historical/models/` contains relaxed replicas for the separate `vantagemovershistorical` DB, not runtime API models.
- `scripts/google_sheets/` — Sheet inspection, diagnostics, auth helpers, structure copy, and service-account utilities.
- `scripts/postman/` — Postman login and collection/environment sync for API tooling.
- `scripts/ringcentral/` — Manual diagnostics, webhook subscription management, Call Log validation/probes, workflow tests, and manual cron/reconcile runners. Keep reusable runtime logic in `src/services/ringcentral/` and call it from scripts.
- `scripts/dev_ops/google_apps_scripts/` — Google Apps Script form helpers; `scripts/demos/` — runnable demos/fixtures; `scripts/docs/` — generated source-workbook documentation.

## Working Rules

- Preserve live workflow boundaries: form leads, call leads, bookings, cancellations, customers, agents/receiver attribution, CRM submission, Google Sheets sync, RingCentral ingest, Granot extension enrichment/reconciliation/CSV, reconciliation, enrichment, historical backfill, analytics, and Postman collection management are separate concerns even when they share models.
- Prefer adding focused modules inside the existing domain folders over expanding broad orchestration files or `v1.routes.ts` handler blocks.
- Keep side effects explicit: Mongo is the source of truth; CRM, Google Sheets, S3/Granot CSV storage, Postman, and historical workbooks are external targets that need mode-aware logging and safe identifiers.
- Use `pnpm test` for `src/**/*.test.ts` and `pnpm typecheck` after runtime TypeScript changes when practical.
